WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.667 --> 00:00:17.990
I'd lived at Birtwick Park for several years and was happy there.

2
00:00:17.991 --> 00:00:21.440
Even Ginger was content now.

3
00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:26.683
But sad changes were coming. The mistress was ill more and more often.

4
00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:32.376
The doctor was at the house a lot, and the squire always looked worried and distracted.

5
00:00:32.377 --> 00:00:37.073
"Did you hear the news?" John asked Little Joe one day in the stable.

6
00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:40.282
"What news?" Little Joe asked.

7
00:00:40.283 --> 00:00:43.516
"It's the mistress," John said sadly.

8
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:47.311
"The doctor says her health will only get worse if she stays here.

9
00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:50.398
She needs to move to a warmer place right away.

10
00:00:50.399 --> 00:00:53.370
The whole family will be leaving soon."

11
00:00:53.371 --> 00:00:58.364
"Oh no!" Little Joe's face went pale. "Poor mistress.

12
00:00:58.365 --> 00:01:01.841
And what's going to happen to the rest of us?"

13
00:01:01.842 --> 00:01:07.500
"I don't know. I guess we'll find out soon enough."

14
00:01:07.501 --> 00:01:11.626
After that John was always silent and sad as he worked.

15
00:01:11.627 --> 00:01:16.335
Little Joe hardly ever whistled anymore.

16
00:01:16.336 --> 00:01:23.778
People came and went from the estate more often than usual, and Ginger and I had plenty of work carrying them around.

17
00:01:23.779 --> 00:01:30.267
The first people to leave Birtwick Park were the squire's young daughters, Miss Jessie and Miss Flora.

18
00:01:30.268 --> 00:01:37.166
The two little girls came to say good-bye to all of us horses, especially Merrylegs, their favorite.

19
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:41.277
They hugged him so tightly, I thought they'd never let go.

20
00:01:41.278 --> 00:01:45.766
When their nanny pulled them away, both girls were crying.

21
00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:50.496
John and Little Joe looked sadder than ever as they watched the girls leave.

22
00:01:50.497 --> 00:01:53.992
"I suppose that's the beginning of the end," John said.

23
00:01:53.993 --> 00:01:57.050
"Soon the whole family will be gone."

24
00:01:57.051 --> 00:02:01.300
"What will happen to Merrylegs now?" Little Joe asked.

25
00:02:01.301 --> 00:02:05.042
"The squire says the minister wants him," John replied.

26
00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:10.295
"He needs a pony for his housekeeper to ride on errands, and Merrylegs is perfect for the job.

27
00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:15.125
The minister promised never to sell him, but to keep him for the rest of his life."

28
00:02:15.126 --> 00:02:20.012
"That sounds good." Little Joe looked at Ginger and me.

29
00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:22.494
"What about the other horses?"

30
00:02:22.495 --> 00:02:28.424
"The squire already agreed to sell Black Beauty and Ginger to an old friend of his," John said.

31
00:02:28.425 --> 00:02:30.643
"They'll have a good home."

32
00:02:30.644 --> 00:02:35.852
I looked at Ginger, and she at me. This was the first we'd heard about it.

33
00:02:35.853 --> 00:02:38.210
I wasn't sure how to feel.

34
00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:42.893
I'd miss Birtwick Park, but I was glad to have a place to go.

35
00:02:42.894 --> 00:02:48.839
Later we heard that the minister wanted Little Joe to come and work for him and take care of Merrylegs.

36
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:53.605
I was glad. Both of them would be happy to have a familiar face around.

37
00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:57.312
The squire had found new homes for his other horses too.

38
00:02:57.313 --> 00:03:01.185
Soon it was almost time for the squire and his wife to leave.

39
00:03:01.186 --> 00:03:06.539
The squire came to the stable to give us horses a last pat.

40
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.299
"Have you decided what to do with yourself, John?" he asked.

41
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:14.212
"I think I want to become a horse trainer," John said.

42
00:03:14.213 --> 00:03:18.300
"I've seen so many horses ruined by bad early training.

43
00:03:18.301 --> 00:03:22.018
I'd love to fix the ruined ones and give others a good start."

44
00:03:22.019 --> 00:03:26.633
"I can't think of anyone better for that kind of job," the squire said.

45
00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.588
"I'll write to some friends of mine about you.

46
00:03:28.589 --> 00:03:32.007
I'm sure they can help you get started."

47
00:03:32.008 --> 00:03:37.698
John thanked him, and the squire thanked him in return for his years of faithful service.

48
00:03:37.699 --> 00:03:41.537
For a moment neither man seemed to know what else to say.

49
00:03:41.538 --> 00:03:43.533
Then it was time to go.

50
00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:48.715
The other servants had taken most of the luggage away the day before.

51
00:03:48.716 --> 00:03:55.094
When Ginger and I pulled the carriage to the front door of the house, there were only a few bags and trunks to load.

52
00:03:55.095 --> 00:03:58.997
Then the squire came out carrying his wife in his arms.

53
00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:03.380
He set her gently inside the carriage, and then climbed in himself.

54
00:04:03.381 --> 00:04:08.779
With a last good-bye to the remaining servants, we were off.

55
00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:12.895
It didn't take long to reach the nearest railroad station.

56
00:04:12.896 --> 00:04:17.286
When we got there, the mistress climbed out of the carriage on her own.

57
00:04:17.287 --> 00:04:21.997
"Good-bye, John," she said in her soft, sweet voice.

58
00:04:21.998 --> 00:04:29.813
"Thank you for everything. We'll miss you."

59
00:04:29.814 --> 00:04:35.677
Little Joe had climbed out to stand by our heads while the railway workers unloaded the luggage.

60
00:04:35.678 --> 00:04:39.703
I could see tears running down his face.

61
00:04:39.704 --> 00:04:42.802
Soon the train came puffing into the station.

62
00:04:42.803 --> 00:04:50.224
There was lots of hustle and bustle for a few minutes with people getting on and off, and workers running around.

63
00:04:50.225 --> 00:04:55.694
Then a whistle blew and the train chugged away again, leaving behind nothing but smoke.

64
00:04:55.695 --> 00:05:01.666
John watched the whole time. When the train disappeared, he sighed.

65
00:05:01.667 --> 00:05:06.268
"We'll never see her again," he said quietly. "Never."

66
00:05:06.269 --> 00:05:13.966
He and Little Joe climbed back onto the carriage, and we set off for home—only it wasn't our home anymore.

67
00:05:13.967 --> 00:05:21.188
No, Birtwick Park would never be our home again.
